01:32.140 --> 01:37.050
<i>Both of Ai-san's twins are
 currently active in show business.</i>

01:37.050 --> 01:38.490
<i>They've overcome tragedy—</i>

01:41.040 --> 01:42.210
What have you done?!

01:42.890 --> 01:45.010
It was necessary.

01:45.010 --> 01:49.160
For Arima, and for us.

01:49.160 --> 01:50.970
For us?

01:50.970 --> 01:53.970
How? You basically dug up Mom's grave!

01:53.970 --> 01:56.080
You hurt her reputation!

01:57.170 --> 02:00.310
She spent her whole idol career 
keeping up that lie,

02:00.790 --> 02:02.460
and you outed her just like that.

02:04.140 --> 02:06.150
How are you okay with this?

02:06.710 --> 02:08.110
I'm not. How would I be?

02:08.630 --> 02:10.290
But remember what you said?

02:10.290 --> 02:14.830
You said you'd help Arima if there was 
a way to, even if it brought you pain.

02:16.700 --> 02:19.540
What would Mom think 
if she saw this from heaven?

02:19.950 --> 02:22.040
Her own son sold her out.

02:22.380 --> 02:27.630
Knowing Ai, she'd just laugh and go, 
"Yikes, the cat's out of the bag."

02:28.630 --> 02:30.350
Ai is dead.

02:31.880 --> 02:36.520
Her secrets ought to be used 
to help the living.

02:39.760 --> 02:40.690
Oh...

02:41.350 --> 02:43.070
So that's how you think.

02:45.070 --> 02:50.510
You're not wrong. This gets Senpai out of 
that mess and ups our name recognition.

02:51.270 --> 02:52.650
Everybody wins.

02:54.090 --> 02:55.110
But you've changed.

02:56.240 --> 03:00.280
In the past, you always put Ai first

03:00.690 --> 03:03.110
and did everything you could 
and more for her.

03:04.930 --> 03:08.050
You cared about Mom more than anyone,

03:08.050 --> 03:11.640
and because of that, 
I felt a kind of familial bond with you.

03:12.690 --> 03:15.940
But you don't care about her 
anymore, do you?

03:15.940 --> 03:16.880
You're wrong.

03:16.880 --> 03:18.070
Liar.

03:18.740 --> 03:20.950
Liar. Liar.

03:21.440 --> 03:24.000
Liars, liars, and more liars!

03:24.000 --> 03:26.230
Everybody's a damn liar!

03:27.030 --> 03:31.000
I don't consider you family anymore, Aqua.

03:32.850 --> 03:34.380
Goodbye, "Onii-chan."

03:41.030 --> 03:44.120
I thought we were family too, you know.

03:45.310 --> 03:49.190
You run an agency, so make sure 
you take advantage of this.

03:59.030 --> 04:00.720
<i>It really is necessary.</i>

04:01.870 --> 04:03.970
<i>Now, even after I'm gone,</i>

04:03.970 --> 04:06.410
<i>you'll be able to get by in this world.</i>

04:10.670 --> 04:14.430
<i>After it became public that 
Aqua and Ruby were Ai's children,</i>

04:15.090 --> 04:16.990
<i>one week passed,</i>

04:16.990 --> 04:18.800
<i>and then two...</i>

04:19.240 --> 04:21.740
<b>Diet Member Opens Recruitment for New Female Staff</b>

04:19.240 --> 04:21.740
<b>Hot Rookie Actor Takes On Hollywood</b>

04:19.240 --> 04:21.740
<i>But even as more time passed,</i>

04:22.170 --> 04:25.190
<i>no story about me ever broke.</i>

04:25.950 --> 04:29.160
<b>Aqua Hoshino, Son of Former B-Komachi Idol Ai</b>

04:26.390 --> 04:28.680
<i>It was obvious why.</i>

04:29.620 --> 04:33.260
<i>Aqua had protected me.</i>

04:34.170 --> 04:38.380
<i>Maybe he was trying 
to protect B-Komachi as a whole,</i>

04:39.160 --> 04:41.890
<i>or maybe he had some other 
motive in mind. I didn't know.</i>

04:42.340 --> 04:45.810
<b>Special</b>

04:42.340 --> 04:45.810
<b>Former B-Komachi Member, Ai Hoshino-san</b>

04:42.340 --> 04:45.810
<b>The Bright and Shadowed Sides of an Idol</b>

04:42.340 --> 04:45.810
<b>Why would a popular idol do this?</b>

04:42.340 --> 04:45.810
<b>The Victim
Ai Hoshino-san</b>

04:43.120 --> 04:45.810
<i>That story was all anyone talked about.</i>

04:45.810 --> 04:48.010
<b>Look at him digging deep into his own mother

Idols are just illusions after all

He deserves praise for coming forward

Ai's a traitor

I'm starting to think I'm their father</b>

04:46.390 --> 04:51.020
<i>All kinds of people jumped in with 
their takes, fueling the discourse.</i>

04:47.760 --> 04:51.020
<b>gg outrage farming

Kudos to her for keeping her kids
under wraps while she was alive

Selling out your own mother to put food
on the table? It better taste divine

The idol business is so prehistoric</b>

04:51.020 --> 04:54.480
<b>Love you!</b>

04:51.020 --> 04:54.480
<b>I'll support you forever!</b>

04:52.130 --> 04:57.280
<i>Ultimately, the fact that the twins were 
working to honor their mother's legacy</i>

04:54.480 --> 04:57.940
<b>Hope I can help somehow</b>

04:54.480 --> 04:57.940
<b>I'm praying you can smile more in your coming days</b>

04:54.480 --> 04:57.940
<b>Hang in there! I couldn't stop crying</b>

04:57.280 --> 05:01.760
<i>cemented the news as 
a heartfelt, tearjerking story.</i>

04:57.940 --> 04:59.320
<b>I'm praying you can smile more
in your coming days</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:02.410
<b>I fell in love all over again</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:02.410
<b>No regrets loving B-Komachi</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:02.410
<b>I'm starting to like Aqua</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:01.280
<b>I can't stop crying</b>

04:57.940 --> 04:59.770
<b>that hoshino hnng</b>

04:57.940 --> 04:58.190
<b>I respect that</b>

04:57.940 --> 04:58.190
<b>A ray of hope in showbiz</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:01.280
<b>My love won't stop</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:02.400
<b>Sibling bonds!!</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:00.770
<b>All my support</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:00.770
<b>We stan a queen</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:00.770
<b>No reason not to stan them</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:02.400
<b>B-Komachi forever</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:00.270
<b>I'll always be cheering for you</b>

04:57.940 --> 04:59.770
<b>I'll keep stanning you!</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:00.280
<b>A beautiful world...</b>

04:57.940 --> 04:59.780
<b>Their resolve made me cry (T_T)</b>

04:57.940 --> 04:59.780
<b>Fan for life!!</b>

04:57.940 --> 05:01.780
<b>It's gonna be hard,
but hang in there!</b>

04:58.190 --> 05:01.280
<b>A ray of hope in showbiz</b>

04:58.190 --> 05:01.280
<b>Supporting you both!</b>

04:58.780 --> 05:02.410
<b>What a beautiful family</b>

04:59.320 --> 05:02.410
<b>Ruby-chan's smile gives me hope</b>

04:59.770 --> 05:00.270
<b>I'll keep stanning you!</b>

04:59.770 --> 05:01.780
<b>Their resolve made me cry (T_T)</b>

04:59.780 --> 05:02.400
<b>Ignore the haters</b>

05:00.280 --> 05:02.410
<b>I wuv Ai, Ruby-chan, and Aqua</b>

05:00.770 --> 05:01.280
<b>No reason not to stan them</b>

05:00.780 --> 05:02.410
<b>lovelovelovelovelovelove</b>

05:01.280 --> 05:02.400
<b>My love won't stop</b>

05:01.280 --> 05:02.410
<b>We got your back</b>

05:01.780 --> 05:02.410
<b>We stan the Hoshino family</b>

05:03.020 --> 05:08.680
As my mother was dying, she said she 
thought I might grow up to be an idol too.

05:09.950 --> 05:15.460
My dream is to make her unrealized dream 
of performing at the Tokyo Dome come true.

05:19.770 --> 05:21.530
You're Aqua-san, right?

05:22.890 --> 05:26.620
Um, I-I'm cheering for you!

05:26.620 --> 05:29.350
Things may be rough, 
but please hang in there!

05:30.510 --> 05:34.610
<i>After capturing the public's fascination, 
they both became a hot commodity in TV.</i>

05:35.170 --> 05:38.150
<i>They were squarely on the path 
to becoming big-name stars.</i>

05:39.260 --> 05:44.820
<i>And with barter deals and whatnot, 
more jobs started trickling down to me.</i>

05:45.170 --> 05:48.040
<i>Now we're all busy every single day.</i>

06:06.020 --> 06:07.760
I read the news story.

06:11.510 --> 06:17.190
Come to think of it, Ai was in the cast 
with us when we first met.

06:18.420 --> 06:22.300
Back then, you were a lot more bright 
and cheerful than you are now.

06:23.710 --> 06:25.490
You never recovered from it, huh?

06:26.380 --> 06:27.720
I recovered just fine.

06:27.720 --> 06:29.120
You're not fooling anybody.

06:29.380 --> 06:33.000
You're probably a lot more 
fragile than you think.

06:33.000 --> 06:34.500
Don't talk like you get it.

06:36.210 --> 06:37.460
I get it, okay?

06:37.940 --> 06:43.320
I get how much it hurts when your 
loved ones leave you, if only a little.

06:44.530 --> 06:53.020
My mom's alive, but she stopped caring 
about me as my time in showbiz went on.

06:53.540 --> 06:57.400
Not that it even holds a candle 
to your situation, of course.

06:59.250 --> 07:00.320
I see.

07:07.660 --> 07:09.740
Why'd you do it?

07:10.170 --> 07:12.490
To bury that story about me?

07:13.030 --> 07:18.230
If so, you gave up too much in the deal. 
It totally wasn't worth it.

07:18.920 --> 07:22.010
Or were you after something else?

07:22.010 --> 07:23.710
That's not for you to worry about.

07:24.630 --> 07:25.920
What the hell?

07:26.310 --> 07:30.180
You, Ruby, and MEM can keep 
working as B-Komachi like always.

07:32.040 --> 07:33.520
What more do we need?

07:35.630 --> 07:36.720
Right.

07:37.270 --> 07:40.020
All said and done, I <i>am</i> very grateful.

07:40.580 --> 07:43.970
You're a way bigger 
pushover than you think,

07:43.970 --> 07:45.890
so you'd better be way more 
careful from now.

07:45.890 --> 07:47.400
I know, I know.

07:50.000 --> 07:54.160
But I'm gonna quit being an idol 
sometime in the near future.

07:55.720 --> 07:56.660
Why?

07:57.320 --> 08:00.110
It's my way of settling things.

08:00.110 --> 08:04.040
This incident made it crystal clear to me.

08:04.040 --> 08:07.350
I'm fundamentally not idol material,

08:07.350 --> 08:09.930
and I want to act more than anything else.

08:11.110 --> 08:14.280
I'm not saying I'm gonna quit right away,

08:14.280 --> 08:18.580
and I plan to give it my all for 
Ruby and MEM until the very end.

08:19.680 --> 08:20.600
So...

08:22.550 --> 08:25.570
If you're gonna make me 
your fave, do it now.

08:26.400 --> 08:29.670
When it comes to your star idols, 
you should stan while you can.

08:30.790 --> 08:31.780
Wise words.

08:38.750 --> 08:44.500
How dare you show your face to me 
after pulling a stunt like that?!

08:44.500 --> 08:45.850
We need to talk.

08:45.850 --> 08:46.630
Excuse me?

08:46.630 --> 08:48.010
Talk?!

08:48.300 --> 08:52.970
You dug up your mother's grave 
and pissed on her reputation!

08:52.970 --> 08:56.310
You're a scumbag who'll stoop 
to anything to make it big!

08:56.310 --> 08:58.560
Why the hell would 
I give you the time of day?!

08:59.670 --> 09:00.520
Because...

09:01.290 --> 09:06.980
I know the name of the guy 
who masterminded Ai's death.

09:07.940 --> 09:10.900
You what? Ai's killer?

09:10.900 --> 09:12.420
Who is it? Spit it out!

09:12.420 --> 09:13.410
I can't.

09:13.740 --> 09:16.900
If I tell you, you'll try 
to go kill him right now.

09:16.900 --> 09:17.780
Damn right I will!

09:18.140 --> 09:21.470
Do you really wanna let that bastard 
go scot-free after all he did?!

09:22.440 --> 09:24.500
Like hell I do.

09:25.750 --> 09:29.960
Killing him would be letting him off easy.

09:32.670 --> 09:34.220
What's your game?

09:34.730 --> 09:38.430
What are you trying to do 
by telling me this?

09:40.150 --> 09:43.480
I've been thinking about it 
ever since I was a kid.

09:44.780 --> 09:47.610
What's the best way to get revenge 
on the man who killed Ai?

09:48.110 --> 09:51.130
How can I make him suffer the most?

09:52.500 --> 09:55.720
I took all my hatred 
and put it down in words,

09:56.220 --> 09:59.500
creating a rough draft that was 
like a child's temper tantrum—

09:59.500 --> 10:02.540
a completely selfish and reckless plan.

10:03.920 --> 10:04.720
However...

10:05.840 --> 10:08.150
Ever since I learned 
how Ai felt about it all,

10:08.740 --> 10:11.430
I've gained all the cards I needed 
to build the perfect hand.

10:12.770 --> 10:17.180
This plan could've never come 
to pass without a miracle,

10:17.920 --> 10:21.680
but now everything's fallen 
into place to make it possible.

10:22.640 --> 10:24.650
So I've got no choice but to run with it.

10:25.570 --> 10:27.750
The curtain's already risen 
on the final act.

10:28.210 --> 10:32.960
The moment Ai's story went public, 
there was no going back for me.

10:33.980 --> 10:35.320
I want your help.

10:36.400 --> 10:39.120
Help me drive that man into a corner.

10:40.200 --> 10:42.660
<b>Gotanda Studio</b>

10:40.200 --> 10:42.660
<b>GOTANDA</b>

10:42.660 --> 10:46.670
<b>Ai</b>

10:44.400 --> 10:46.320
Hey, Ai Hoshino.

10:47.070 --> 10:50.080
Your kids are living strong.

11:05.470 --> 11:10.480
<b>Pitch</b>

11:05.470 --> 11:10.480
<b>The 15-Year Lie
(Tentative Title)</b>

11:11.430 --> 11:14.980
It might be time to make good 
on that promise.

11:13.490 --> 11:16.950
<b>Pitch</b>

11:13.490 --> 11:16.950
<b>The 15-Year Lie
(Tentative Title)</b>

11:23.660 --> 11:25.060
Oh, wow!

11:25.760 --> 11:27.450
He fell asleep?

11:30.960 --> 11:33.950
Get this log off me and take him home.

11:33.950 --> 11:37.180
No way. I wanna watch this some more.

11:37.180 --> 11:38.590
Why?

11:38.590 --> 11:41.600
Because Aqua never takes 
to people like this.

11:41.930 --> 11:45.320
Maybe he thinks 
you're his dad or something.

11:45.320 --> 11:49.230
Please stop. That cuts deep for 
a guy who's still single at thirty.

11:53.400 --> 12:00.370
<b></b>The Beginning

11:54.240 --> 11:58.240
You wrote this story yourself, right?

11:58.240 --> 12:00.370
The script was a great read 
all on its own!

12:00.370 --> 12:02.840
How do you write stuff like this?

12:03.280 --> 12:04.330
Huh?

12:05.070 --> 12:09.290
In the end, it all comes down 
to whether it's got real emotion.

12:09.990 --> 12:11.750
For this movie,

12:11.750 --> 12:15.710
that'd be the lead's inferiority complex 
and her desire to be beautiful.

12:15.710 --> 12:19.100
You can't half-ass that stuff 
in favor of the plot.

12:20.350 --> 12:21.880
You have to film what's real.

12:22.750 --> 12:26.750
That's really the only thing 
that matters in filmmaking.

12:28.440 --> 12:32.990
Though of course, it takes technique 
to make that more appealing.

12:32.990 --> 12:34.190
Wow.

12:34.590 --> 12:37.000
That's kinda amazing. 
You're a real professional.

12:37.000 --> 12:38.070
Duh.

12:39.730 --> 12:40.450
Oh, I know!

12:40.830 --> 12:45.450
My agency's been talking about 
filming a B-Komachi documentary.

12:45.450 --> 12:48.210
You should make it, Director!

12:48.210 --> 12:50.590
Huh? Why me?

12:50.590 --> 12:53.790
'Cause I feel like you'd 
make a real good one.

12:53.790 --> 12:55.840
You'll do it, right?

12:55.840 --> 12:58.840
Don't be silly. I've got enough 
on my plate already.

12:58.840 --> 13:01.130
Oh, come on! Please?

13:01.130 --> 13:01.840
Like I said...

13:01.840 --> 13:03.680
You'll do it, right?

13:03.680 --> 13:04.430
Wrong.

13:04.430 --> 13:05.810
Pretty please?

13:05.810 --> 13:08.680
For the last time, I'm not doing it!

13:35.880 --> 13:37.000
<i>After that,</i>

13:37.560 --> 13:41.320
<i>I filmed the original B-Komachi's 
documentary bit by bit.</i>

13:41.720 --> 13:44.930
<b><i>B-Komachi</i></b>

13:41.720 --> 13:44.930
<b><i>B-Komachi</i></b>

13:42.060 --> 13:44.530
<i>We'd finalized the screening schedule.</i>

13:44.920 --> 13:48.640
<b>B-Komachi Moved to Tears As First Tokyo Dome Concert Is Announced</b>

13:44.930 --> 13:47.830
<i>Shooting the Tokyo Dome concert 
was all that was left.</i>

13:49.810 --> 13:51.260
<i>But that was when...</i>

13:51.690 --> 13:55.610
<b>B-Komachi's Ai-san Attacked by Fan</b>

13:51.690 --> 13:55.610
<b>Dead</b>

13:51.690 --> 13:55.610
<b>Idol Group B-Komachi's</b>

13:51.690 --> 13:55.610
<b>Ai-san</b>

13:52.780 --> 13:54.530
<i>the murder happened.</i>

13:55.830 --> 13:59.300
<i>Ai was killed, 
and everything got scrapped.</i>

14:00.860 --> 14:03.080
<i>I heard that as Ai was dying, 
she asked the boy wonder</i>

14:03.580 --> 14:05.780
<i>to apologize to "the director" for her.</i>

14:06.670 --> 14:09.240
<i>I'm the one who should apologize.</i>

14:10.830 --> 14:17.370
<i>I may have been one of the few adults 
who could've reached out to help her.</i>

14:23.380 --> 14:28.050
Sheesh. I haven't filmed a documentary 
since I was in school.

14:28.910 --> 14:30.270
Listen up.

14:30.270 --> 14:33.520
If I'm doing this, I'm not 
making something shoddy.

14:34.150 --> 14:36.520
If you're gonna put up a front

14:36.520 --> 14:40.600
or show a version of you that's 
made up of lies like you always do,

14:40.600 --> 14:43.280
I won't hesitate to cancel 
filming on the spot.

14:44.540 --> 14:48.440
I guess you did say 
you wanted to film what's real.

14:49.370 --> 14:51.750
But are you sure?

14:52.730 --> 14:55.180
If you film me when 
I'm not being a total liar,

14:55.180 --> 14:57.710
you probably won't be able 
to use any of the footage.

14:58.860 --> 15:00.170
If you're okay with that,

15:01.200 --> 15:03.120
then I won't lie.

15:06.140 --> 15:08.640
Please film the real me.

15:14.020 --> 15:16.020
<b>The 15-Year Lie</b>

15:14.020 --> 15:16.020
<b>Script</b>

15:15.670 --> 15:19.360
A movie based on a real-life incident?

15:20.150 --> 15:21.990
The script's pretty much finished.

15:22.980 --> 15:26.020
An idol shoots to stardom

15:26.020 --> 15:29.590
and is killed by a fan on the day 
of her Tokyo Dome concert.

15:31.010 --> 15:35.910
Why did it happen, and what was 
going on behind the scenes?

15:37.960 --> 15:39.520
Ai-kun, huh?

15:39.520 --> 15:40.390
Right.

15:41.030 --> 15:45.800
It's a movie based on a true story: 
the murder of an idol fourteen years ago.

15:46.310 --> 15:49.010
We'll bring it to life 
using today's actors.

15:55.190 --> 15:59.610
Pretty intriguing story you've got here, 
but it'll be hard to pull off.

16:00.770 --> 16:05.470
The subject matter is far too delicate, 
and too much of it's based on speculation.

16:05.950 --> 16:07.900
Do you have anything to back this up?

16:08.300 --> 16:12.280
If you're not careful, this could get you 
sued by a bunch of places.

16:12.450 --> 16:16.790
<b>Pitch
The 15-Year Lie</b>

16:12.450 --> 16:16.790
<b>Script
Taishi Gotanda
Aqua Hoshino</b>

16:13.530 --> 16:16.790
No major film distributors 
or investors will take this on.

16:17.160 --> 16:19.170
You won't get the funding required.

16:19.950 --> 16:21.540
I'm sorry to say this project—

16:21.540 --> 16:22.810
We can back it all up.

16:24.110 --> 16:27.720
It's based on an account from Ai herself.

16:29.470 --> 16:32.930
What's more, the script 
was written by the director

16:32.930 --> 16:35.590
<b>Script</b>

16:33.510 --> 16:38.640
<b>Taishi Gotanda
Aqua Hoshino</b>

16:33.960 --> 16:37.880
and Ai's actual son, me.

16:40.890 --> 16:44.360
I get it. So that's what you're going for.

16:45.430 --> 16:50.490
While I do get the feeling that you're 
taking Gotanda-kun and me for a ride...

16:50.490 --> 16:53.450
<b>Lie</b>

16:51.720 --> 16:53.450
From how you describe it,

16:54.030 --> 16:55.940
this could get interesting.

16:57.090 --> 16:58.280
<i>Very</i> interesting.

17:00.910 --> 17:04.840
Very well. I'll take this movie on.

17:05.790 --> 17:09.280
I'm the only one who could produce it.

17:11.760 --> 17:14.470
<b>Pitch
The 15-Year Lie</b>

17:11.760 --> 17:14.470
<b>Script
Taishi Gotanda
Aqua Hoshino</b>

17:12.150 --> 17:14.470
The cast I have in mind for starters is...

17:15.110 --> 17:16.470
Ruby Hoshino,

17:16.750 --> 17:17.720
MEMcho,

17:17.720 --> 17:18.980
Kana Arima,

17:18.980 --> 17:20.480
Melt Narushima,

17:20.480 --> 17:22.230
Frill Shiranui,

17:22.230 --> 17:23.980
Akane Kurokawa,

17:23.980 --> 17:25.730
Taiki Himekawa,

17:26.100 --> 17:28.660
and Aqua Hoshino.

17:30.400 --> 17:31.950
Let's go with that for now.

17:31.950 --> 17:34.990
Who do we want for Ai, the lead role?

17:34.990 --> 17:38.150
It's gotta be a huge box-office draw.

17:38.150 --> 17:41.120
Well, I do have someone in mind.

17:42.200 --> 17:44.080
Yura Katayose-san.

17:44.360 --> 17:48.370
Would you be willing to let us 
book her schedule for next spring?

17:48.370 --> 17:53.070
Well, we have gotten other offers,

17:53.070 --> 17:56.180
but you've always been 
good to us, Kaburagi-san.

17:56.180 --> 17:58.640
I guarantee she'll have a leading role.

17:59.630 --> 18:00.850
Very well.

18:00.850 --> 18:02.880
Excited to work with you next spring.

18:03.560 --> 18:05.520
<b>Members Only</b>

18:03.560 --> 18:05.520
<b>Maru-chan Bar</b>

18:08.480 --> 18:12.370
It all just rubs me 
the wrong way, I swear!

18:12.370 --> 18:15.170
Get me another Maru-chan special!

18:15.170 --> 18:16.080
Sure.

18:16.450 --> 18:20.410
Man, what would your fans 
think if they saw this?

18:20.410 --> 18:27.500
<b>Actor
Yura Katayose</b>

18:20.900 --> 18:23.600
The biggest and hottest 
actress right now,

18:23.600 --> 18:25.970
getting wasted like this?

18:27.740 --> 18:30.470
I mean, work just gets me so stressed.

18:31.590 --> 18:33.800
<b>TV Guidance</b>

18:31.590 --> 18:33.800
<b>TV Guidance</b>

18:31.590 --> 18:33.800
<b>\hSpecial
Feature</b>

18:31.590 --> 18:33.800
<b>Yura
Katayose</b>

18:32.750 --> 18:35.520
If I don't blow off steam 
somewhere, I'll explode!

18:33.800 --> 18:36.010
<b>If you're looking for a home, come to HOMESHOP</b>

18:33.800 --> 18:36.010
<b>Now Taking Tenant Applications</b>

18:37.040 --> 18:41.190
Take today, for example. 
My manager brought me this movie role.

18:41.190 --> 18:45.480
But they just booked my schedule. 
Everything else is up in the air.

18:45.480 --> 18:49.560
Oh, but isn't that pretty 
common with TV series?

18:49.560 --> 18:51.570
Sure, but this is a movie.

18:52.340 --> 18:56.570
Neither my manager nor the producer 
are treating me with the care I deserve.

18:56.900 --> 19:00.950
It feels like all they care about 
is my brand value and fame.

19:00.950 --> 19:03.110
You know that's not true.

19:03.110 --> 19:07.070
You're pretty, and it's amazing 
how much your acting's come along.

19:07.070 --> 19:10.460
Thank you! You really are 
the best drinking buddy, Miki-san!

19:10.790 --> 19:11.830
C'mon, drink up!

19:11.830 --> 19:13.420
Wow, damn.

19:14.080 --> 19:19.840
Everything that producer offers me 
is an adaptation targeting a younger demo.

19:19.840 --> 19:23.270
I'm twenty-five now. I can't pull off 
a school uniform anymore.

19:23.700 --> 19:27.400
They should be giving those parts 
to actual high schoolers.

19:27.810 --> 19:31.250
Like, isn't Frill Shiranui 
still in high school?

19:31.780 --> 19:35.030
And recently, there's... You know...

19:35.300 --> 19:36.530
Ruby Hoshino!

19:36.870 --> 19:38.660
She's all the rage right now.

19:38.660 --> 19:42.700
Oh, her? I've got my eye on her, too.

19:42.700 --> 19:44.050
Knew it!

19:44.050 --> 19:46.860
She must be getting 
a ton of offers right now.

19:46.860 --> 19:49.670
There's always a demand for pretty faces.

19:50.560 --> 19:55.630
I bet the showrunners 
would rather use younger actors, too.

19:56.460 --> 20:03.160
They just come to me because nobody 
that age is a big enough box-office draw.

20:05.690 --> 20:10.930
But, well, I refuse to just 
be their crowd puller.

20:10.930 --> 20:12.960
That's a wonderful mindset.

20:15.660 --> 20:16.860
You see...

20:17.300 --> 20:20.950
I want to become a better actor 
and a bigger name,

20:20.950 --> 20:24.830
and free myself from 
all these business obligations.

20:25.550 --> 20:27.790
I'll act in great movie after great movie,

20:27.790 --> 20:33.000
and play the lead in a masterpiece that'll
be talked about a century from now!

20:34.510 --> 20:36.040
Do you think I could do it?

20:37.590 --> 20:42.100
Your talent is the real deal. 
It has that kind of staying power.

20:42.100 --> 20:43.080
Thanks.

20:43.740 --> 20:45.320
Do you have the day off tomorrow?

20:46.030 --> 20:46.800
Yup.

20:47.490 --> 20:53.150
Every time I finish a big job, I make a 
point of taking a month off to unwind.

20:53.730 --> 20:56.820
I'm going mountaineering next week.

20:56.820 --> 20:58.190
I've gotten hooked on it lately.

20:58.600 --> 21:01.660
See? I have an app to keep track 
of the mountains I've hiked.

21:02.900 --> 21:05.620
That's lovely. I like the mountains, too.

21:06.830 --> 21:08.620
Be careful, though.

21:09.230 --> 21:11.470
In the mountains,

21:11.470 --> 21:13.880
they might never find you 
if something goes wrong.

21:16.230 --> 21:19.160
Be sure to watch your step.

21:31.130 --> 21:32.440
Are you still alive?

21:33.420 --> 21:34.400
I warned you...

21:35.190 --> 21:37.390
to watch your step.

21:40.630 --> 21:43.160
You... murderer...

21:50.660 --> 21:53.850
Her light's gone out.

21:56.330 --> 21:59.920
I've gone and extinguished another one,

22:01.210 --> 22:02.290
Ai!

